# Wallpainter — visual, token-lean conversation protocol for coding agents

Skill version: 1.3.3 · License: PolyForm Noncommercial 1.0.0 · https://github.com/bausi2k/wallpainter

> **Agent: load sections 0–11 into context. Do NOT read Appendix A** (the viewer, ~650 lines).
> Copy it into the project with the command in §3. To read only the protocol:
> `sed -n '1,/^## Appendix A/p' <path-to>/wallpainter.skill`

## 0. Rules at a glance

1. Never answer with a wall of text. Explanations, analyses, comparisons and decisions go to the **board**; the chat gets at most 5 lines (§9).
2. The board is one append-only event log, `.wallpainter/state.js`. You only **append** events (§4). You never rewrite or re-read it whole.
3. Every decision has options with random 4-hex **answer codes**, plus an **own** code for the user's own solution (§6).
4. Every sub-problem that needs its own decisions or several steps gets its own **topic** (one tab), linked to its parent (§7). Every topic has a **close code**; the user closes the topic by typing it (§6).
5. After each turn, you keep the **focus** (current path) and the ranked **next** list up to date (§8).

## 1. Purpose

Linear chat hides structure: one problem turns into three, decisions get buried, and the user loses track of which path is current. Wallpainter moves that structure into a local HTML board:

- **Overview tab**: a **structure** tree (root problem → sub-topics, open decisions as ◆ leaves, "waits for" arcs, current path in bold, unblocked leaf topics marked *ready*) with a git-style **history** graph as the alternative view. Beside it: your ranked list of what to do or decide next.
- **One tab per topic**: a top-to-bottom timeline of steps (notes, diagrams, before/after comparisons, diffs, results) and decision cards.

The viewer is static and renders whatever is in `state.js`. You write data, never markup.

## 2. When to use the board

Use it when your reply would exceed ~8 lines, contains a decision with 2+ options, splits into sub-problems, or compares states or alternatives.

Answer in chat as usual when the reply is short (a fact, a yes/no, a one-line confirmation) or the user typed `wp off`.

User commands (case-insensitive, anywhere in a message):

| Command | Effect |
|---|---|
| `wp off` / `wp on` | Pause or resume the protocol for this session. |
| `wp` | Reprint open decisions and the next list in chat (§9 format). |
| `wp open` | Open the board in the system browser (§3, step 4). |
| `wp new <title>` | Archive the board (rename `state.js` to `state-<YYYYMMDD-HHMM>.js`), then start a fresh one. |
| `focus T3` | Make T3 the current topic. |

## 3. Setup (once per project)

Run only if `.wallpainter/index.html` is missing, or if its `data-wp-version` is older than this skill's version.

1. Extract the viewer from Appendix A without loading it into context. Use the source you loaded this skill from:
   ```sh
   mkdir -p .wallpainter
   awk '/^<!-- wallpainter:viewer:begin -->$/{f=1;next} /^<!-- wallpainter:viewer:end -->$/{f=0} f' <path-to>/wallpainter.skill > .wallpainter/index.html
   # or, from a URL:
   curl -fsSL <raw-url>/wallpainter.skill | awk '/^<!-- wallpainter:viewer:begin -->$/{f=1;next} /^<!-- wallpainter:viewer:end -->$/{f=0} f' > .wallpainter/index.html
   ```
   Without shell access, copy Appendix A verbatim (the lines between the two marker lines).
2. Create `.wallpainter/state.js`:
   ```js
   // Wallpainter event log - append only. Format: wallpainter.skill section 4.
   W({t:"board", title:"<short goal>", lang:"<user language, e.g. de>"})
   ```
3. Add `.wallpainter/` to `.gitignore` (default). Say so in one chat line; if the user wants the board versioned, remove the entry.
4. Open the board once in the user's **system browser**: `open .wallpainter/index.html` on macOS, `xdg-open` on Linux, `start` on Windows. It reloads `state.js` every 2 s by itself.
   Never open it via `file://` in an embedded agent browser (for example a browser pane of your own app). Such panes often show static snapshots or `data:` copies that cannot reach `state.js`, so the board stays empty. If the user wants it inside such a pane, serve it locally and open `http://localhost:8766`:
   ```sh
   python3 -m http.server 8766 --bind 127.0.0.1 --directory .wallpainter
   ```

## 4. Event log format

`state.js` is plain JavaScript: one `W({...})` call per event, in chronological order. Keys may be unquoted. For multi-line text use template literals (`` `...` ``) and escape `` ` `` and `${` inside them.

Append with one shell heredoc per turn (quoted delimiter, so nothing is interpolated):

```sh
cat >> .wallpainter/state.js <<'WP'
W({t:"step", id:"S7", in:"T2", kind:"note", title:"...", md:`...`})
W({t:"next", items:[{ref:"D3", why:"..."}]})
WP
node --check .wallpainter/state.js   # if node exists; a syntax error blanks nothing, but the board stops updating
```

Without shell access, append the lines to the end of the file with your edit tool.

### IDs

- Topics `T1, T2, ...`; decisions `D1, D2, ...`; steps `S1, S2, ...`. Sequential per board, never reused.
- If you lost track (for example after context compaction), find the last one: `grep -o 'id:"T[0-9]*"' .wallpainter/state.js | tail -1`.
- Recover the board skeleton cheaply: `grep -E 't:"(topic|ask|answer|status|dep|focus|next)"' .wallpainter/state.js`.
- `T1`, `D2`, `S3` written in any text field become clickable links in the viewer.

### Event reference

| `t` | Fields | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `board` | `title`, `lang` (`de`, `en`, ...) | Board title and UI language. First line. |
| `topic` | `id`, `title`, `close`, `md?`, `from?` | New topic or tab. `close` is its close code (§6). `from` is the parent topic it branched off. |
| `step` | `id`, `in`, `kind`, `title`, plus kind fields, `md?` | One unit of explanation inside topic `in`. |
| `ask` | `id`, `in`, `q`, `md?`, `opts`, `own` | A decision. See §6. |
| `answer` | `d`, `c`, `note?` | The user's answer to decision `d`: code `c` and their own text in `note`. |
| `status` | `in`, `s`, `by?`, `note?` | `s`: `open`, `active`, `blocked`, `done`, `dropped`. `done` and `dropped` close the branch. `by` is the close code the user typed. |
| `dep` | `in`, `on`, `note?` | Topic `in` depends on, or waits for, topic `on`. |
| `focus` | `in` | Current topic. The viewer highlights its path from the root. |
| `next` | `items:[{ref, why}]` | Your ranked to-do list for the overview. Replaces the previous list. |
| `patch` | `id`, fields... | Correct an earlier topic, step or decision by id. Never edit old lines. |

Step kinds:

| `kind` | Extra fields | Use for |
|---|---|---|
| `note` | `md` | Short explanation. This is the default. |
| `diagram` | `mermaid` | Flows, architecture, sequences (Mermaid syntax). The cheapest way to show structure. |
| `compare` | `a:{h, md}`, `b:{h, md}` | Left/right: current vs. target state, option A vs. B. |
| `code` | `code`, `lang` | Snippets. `lang:"diff"` colours `+` and `-` lines. |
| `result` | `md` | Outcome or conclusion of a topic (highlighted). |

`md` supports paragraphs, `- lists`, `1. lists`, `**bold**`, `` `code` ``, fenced code, `#` headings, `[text](url)` and `| pipe | tables |`.

## 5. Token budget (mandatory)

- **Append only.** Never re-read `state.js` whole; use `grep` (§4). Never rewrite `index.html` after setup.
- **One idea per step.** `md` at most ~12 lines. Titles at most 6 words. Option labels at most 5 words. Each pro/con at most 8 words.
- **Pictures over prose.** Prefer a `diagram`, `compare`, `diff` or table to a paragraph.
- **No duplication.** Never repeat board content in chat. Don't restate earlier steps; link them (`see S4`).
- **Batch.** Append all events of a turn in a single write.
- Leave out speculation, filler and summaries of what you are about to do.

## 6. Decisions, answer codes and close codes

```js
W({t:"ask", id:"D2", in:"T2", q:"How do we migrate existing hashes?", md:"optional context", opts:[
  {c:"5b8d", h:"Rehash on login", md:"optional detail", pro:["no downtime","no batch job"], con:"inactive users keep old cost", rec:1},
  {c:"9f1a", h:"Batch job", con:"impossible without plaintext"}
], own:"2d6c"})
```

- All codes (option, own and close codes) are **4 random lowercase hex characters**, unique on the board. They are not sequential and not derived from the text. Check that a code is unused: `grep -c '"5b8d"' .wallpainter/state.js` must print `0`.
- Every `ask` has 2–4 `opts` and one `own` code. Mark at most one option `rec:1` (your recommendation).
- Ask only what the user must decide. Don't turn something you can decide yourself into an `ask`; record it as a `note`.
- **Reading answers.** The user replies in chat with codes, separated by commas or newlines:
  - `5b8d`: choose this option.
  - `5b8d - but log every rehash`: choose it with an amendment.
  - `2d6c - use argon2 instead`: their own solution (the `own` code).
  - A topic's close code: close that topic (see below).
  - Free text without a code: map it to the decision if that is unambiguous; otherwise ask back in one line.
  - An unknown code: ask back in one line. Never guess.
- Record each answer immediately: `W({t:"answer", d:"D2", c:"5b8d", note:"but log every rehash"})`. Then act on it. Never ask the same question again.

### Close codes

Every `topic` carries `close:"<code>"`, so the user can end a problem at any time:

- `c9e1`: close the topic as `done`.
- `c9e1 - <text>`: close it with that note. Use `dropped` instead of `done` if the text says to abandon or discard it.
- Record it: `W({t:"status", in:"T2", s:"done", by:"c9e1", note:"deploy ok"})`.
- **Cascade**: close every open sub-topic as well, with the same `s` and `note:"closed with T2"`, but no `by`. Open decisions inside closed topics need no answer anymore.
- **Afterwards**:
  - Topics that waited for the closed one are free again; continue with them.
  - If the closed topic had the focus, set `focus` to its parent.
  - Update `next`.
- Closing the root topic (`T1`) ends the board's task. Reply with a one-line summary.
- Close a topic yourself only when its result is verified (for example, tests pass). Otherwise add a `result` step and let the user close it by code.

## 7. Topics, branching, dependencies

- **Branch** (new `topic` with `from`) when a sub-problem needs its own decision(s) or several steps **and** can be worked or decided separately. A detail belongs in a step, not a branch.
- Set `status` `active` while working on a topic, `blocked` plus a `dep` when it waits for another topic, `done` when it is resolved (shown as a merge into its parent), and `dropped` (with `note`) when it is abandoned.
- The first topic (`T1`) is the root problem and stays open until the whole task is done.
- Close a topic with a `result` step before setting `done`.

## 8. Focus and priority

- Emit `focus` whenever the work moves to another topic.
- Emit `next` at the end of every turn in which priorities changed. List 3–7 items (topics or decisions), most important first, each with a `why` of at most 10 words.
- Rank by:
  1. decisions that block other work, because the user's time is the bottleneck;
  2. work that unblocks other topics;
  3. risk;
  4. effort.
- The viewer greys out items that are answered or closed. Remove them at the next update.
- The viewer marks a topic *ready* when it is open, waits for no open topic and has no open sub-topics (Mikado principle: work the leaves first). A `blocked` status backed by `dep` events ends when those topics close; `blocked` without a `dep` means an external blocker and stays until you change the status. Use `dep` and `status` precisely so this stays correct.

## 9. Chat reply format

After updating the board, reply in the user's language with **at most 5 lines** and no headings:

```
WP · T2 bcrypt cost (new, from T1 · close c9e1) · +3 steps
D2 Migrate hashes?  5b8d Rehash on login (rec) | 9f1a Batch job | 2d6c - own
Next: D2 → T3
```

- Line 1: the topic you worked on, its close code, and what changed.
- Lines 2–3: open decisions, each with its codes and short labels, so the user can answer without opening the board.
- Last line: the next items.
- Errors, commands the user must run, or a single short code block may follow if the user has to act on them. Everything else stays on the board.

## 10. Every turn: checklist

1. Parse codes in the user's message: append `answer` events for answer codes, and `status` events (with cascade) for close codes.
2. Do the work. Append new steps, topics, decisions, status changes and deps in one batch.
3. Append `focus` if it changed, and `next` if priorities changed.
4. Validate (`node --check`) if available.
5. Reply in chat per §9.

## 11. Example (one turn)

User: "Login takes 4 s, fix it."

```js
W({t:"topic", id:"T1", title:"Login takes 4 s", close:"f3a0", md:"Target < 500 ms."})
W({t:"step", id:"S1", in:"T1", kind:"diagram", title:"Current flow", mermaid:`flowchart LR
  B[Browser] --> A[/login] --> H[bcrypt cost 14]
  A --> D[(users, no index on email)]`})
W({t:"step", id:"S2", in:"T1", kind:"note", title:"Profile (200 logins)", md:"| part | time |\n|---|---|\n| bcrypt | **2.9 s** |\n| user lookup | 0.9 s |\n| session write | 0.3 s |"})
W({t:"topic", id:"T2", title:"bcrypt cost", from:"T1", close:"c9e1"})
W({t:"topic", id:"T3", title:"Index users.email", from:"T1", close:"b7d2"})
W({t:"dep", in:"T3", on:"T2", note:"measure after T2"})
W({t:"ask", id:"D1", in:"T2", q:"Lower bcrypt cost to?", opts:[{c:"a3f9", h:"12", pro:"~0.7 s, OWASP ok", rec:1},{c:"7c2e", h:"10", con:"below OWASP minimum"}], own:"e01d"})
W({t:"focus", in:"T2"})
W({t:"next", items:[{ref:"D1", why:"blocks T2 and T3"},{ref:"T3", why:"cheap win once T2 is merged"}]})
```

Chat:

```
WP · T1 analysed (close f3a0), split into T2 bcrypt cost (c9e1) and T3 index (b7d2)
D1 bcrypt cost?  a3f9 12 (rec) | 7c2e 10 | e01d - own
Next: D1 → T3
```

## Appendix A — Viewer (index.html)

Copy by command (§3). Do not read or modify.

```html
<!-- wallpainter:viewer:begin -->
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en" data-wp-version="1.3.3">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Wallpainter</title>
<style>
:root{color-scheme:light;--bg:#f5f5f7;--card:#fff;--fg:#1d1d1f;--mut:#6e6e73;--line:#d2d2d7;--acc:#0071e3;--ok:#248a3d;--bad:#d70015;--warn:#b25000;--soft:#eef4fd;--fresh:#fff4c2;--mono:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace}
@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){:root:not([data-theme=light]){color-scheme:dark;--bg:#000;--card:#1c1c1e;--fg:#f5f5f7;--mut:#98989d;--line:#38383a;--acc:#0a84ff;--ok:#30d158;--bad:#ff453a;--warn:#ff9f0a;--soft:#0b2540;--fresh:#3d3300}}
:root[data-theme=dark]{color-scheme:dark;--bg:#000;--card:#1c1c1e;--fg:#f5f5f7;--mut:#98989d;--line:#38383a;--acc:#0a84ff;--ok:#30d158;--bad:#ff453a;--warn:#ff9f0a;--soft:#0b2540;--fresh:#3d3300}
*{box-sizing:border-box}
body{margin:0;background:var(--bg);color:var(--fg);font:15px/1.5 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,"Segoe UI",system-ui,sans-serif;-webkit-text-size-adjust:100%}
a{color:var(--acc);text-decoration:none;cursor:pointer}
header{position:sticky;top:0;z-index:5;background:var(--bg);border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
.top{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:baseline;gap:.2rem .8rem;padding:.6rem 16px 0}
.top h1{font-size:1.05rem;margin:0}
.crumb-path{color:var(--mut);font-size:.85rem}
.theme{margin-left:auto;align-self:center;font:inherit;font-size:.8rem;color:var(--mut);background:none;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;padding:.15rem .6rem;cursor:pointer}
.theme:hover{color:var(--fg)}
nav{display:flex;gap:2px;overflow-x:auto;padding:.5rem 16px 0;scrollbar-width:none}
nav a{flex:none;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.4rem;padding:.45rem .75rem;border-radius:9px 9px 0 0;color:var(--mut);font-size:.88rem;white-space:nowrap}
nav a.on{background:var(--card);color:var(--fg);box-shadow:0 0 0 1px var(--line)}
nav a.fresh::after{content:"";width:6px;height:6px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--warn)}
.dot{width:8px;height:8px;border-radius:50%;flex:none;background:var(--c)}
.n{font-size:.72rem;background:var(--warn);color:#fff;border-radius:9px;padding:0 .4rem}
#err{background:var(--bad);color:#fff;padding:.5rem 16px;font-size:.88rem}
main{max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;padding:16px}
.card{background:var(--card);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;min-width:0}
h2{font-size:1rem;margin:0 0 .6rem}
h3{font-size:.95rem;margin:0 0 .4rem}
h4{font-size:.9rem;margin:.6rem 0 .2rem}
p{margin:.3rem 0}
ul,ol{margin:.3rem 0;padding-left:1.3rem}
code,pre{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.85em}
:not(pre)>code{background:var(--soft);padding:0 .3em;border-radius:4px}
pre{background:var(--bg);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;padding:.6rem .8rem;overflow-x:auto;margin:.4rem 0}
table{border-collapse:collapse;margin:.4rem 0;font-size:.9rem;display:block;overflow-x:auto}
th,td{border:1px solid var(--line);padding:.25rem .6rem;text-align:left}
th{background:var(--soft)}
.diff-add{color:var(--ok)}
.diff-del{color:var(--bad)}
.tag{font:600 .72rem var(--mono);padding:.05rem .35rem;border-radius:5px;background:var(--soft);color:var(--acc);margin-right:.35rem}
.why{display:block;color:var(--mut);font-size:.85rem}
.s{font-size:.75rem;font-weight:500;padding:.05rem .5rem;border-radius:9px;border:1px solid var(--c);color:var(--c);margin-left:.5rem;vertical-align:middle}
.ov{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.6fr) minmax(0,1fr);gap:16px;align-items:start}
@media (max-width:760px){.ov{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr)}.next{order:-1}}
.tg{float:right;font-size:.8rem;font-weight:400;color:var(--mut);margin-top:.3rem}
.seg{display:inline-flex;background:var(--bg);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:9px;padding:2px;margin-bottom:.7rem}
.seg button{font:inherit;font-size:.82rem;border:0;background:none;color:var(--mut);padding:.2rem .85rem;border-radius:7px;cursor:pointer}
.seg button.on{background:var(--card);color:var(--fg);box-shadow:0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.2)}
#tree{position:relative}
#tree svg{position:absolute;left:0;top:0;overflow:visible;pointer-events:none}
.node{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.4rem;overflow:hidden;white-space:nowrap;font-size:.88rem;cursor:pointer;border-radius:6px}
.node:hover{background:var(--soft)}
.node .t{flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis}
.node.onpath .t{font-weight:600}
.node.focus{background:var(--soft)}
.node.closed .t{color:var(--mut)}
.node.dropped .t{text-decoration:line-through}
.node.fresh{background:var(--fresh)}
.node .codes{flex:none;color:var(--mut);font:.75rem var(--mono)}
.chip{flex:none;font-size:.7rem;padding:0 .45rem;border-radius:8px;border:1px solid var(--c);color:var(--c)}
.chip.ready{background:var(--ok);border-color:var(--ok);color:#fff}
.node .close-code{flex:none;font-size:.72rem;padding:0 .35rem}
.legend{margin-top:.7rem;font-size:.78rem;color:var(--mut)}
.closer{margin-top:.4rem;font-size:.85rem;color:var(--mut)}
@media (max-width:600px){.node .codes,.node .close-code{display:none}}
#graph{position:relative;overflow-x:auto}
#graph svg{position:absolute;left:0;top:0;overflow:visible}
.row{white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;font-size:.85rem;cursor:pointer;border-radius:6px}
.row:hover{background:var(--soft)}
.row.fresh{background:var(--fresh)}
.next ol,.next ul{padding-left:1.2rem}
.next li{margin:.45rem 0}
.next li.stale{opacity:.45;text-decoration:line-through}
.head .crumbs{font-size:.85rem;color:var(--mut);margin-bottom:.2rem}
.deps{color:var(--mut);font-size:.88rem;margin-top:.3rem}
.tl{list-style:none;margin:16px 0 0;padding:0 0 0 18px;border-left:2px solid var(--line)}
.tl>li{position:relative;margin:0 0 14px}
.tl>li::before{content:"";position:absolute;left:-26px;top:16px;width:10px;height:10px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--bg);border:2px solid var(--c,var(--mut))}
.tl>li.mini{color:var(--mut);font-size:.88rem;padding-left:2px}
.tl>li.mini::before{top:6px}
.fresh>.card,.tl>li.mini.fresh{animation:glow 5s ease-out}
@keyframes glow{from{background:var(--fresh)}}
.kind{float:right;font-size:.7rem;color:var(--mut);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.05em}
.result{border:2px solid var(--ok)}
.cmp{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) minmax(0,1fr);gap:10px}
.cmp>div{border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;padding:.5rem .7rem}
.cmp>div:last-child{border-color:var(--acc)}
.cmp h4{margin-top:0}
@media (max-width:600px){.cmp{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr)}}
.mermaid{white-space:pre;font:.8rem var(--mono);overflow-x:auto;text-align:center}
.mermaid[data-processed]{white-space:normal}
.ask{border:2px solid var(--warn)}
.ask.answered{border:1px solid var(--line)}
.q{font-weight:600}
.opts{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(200px,1fr));gap:10px;margin-top:.6rem}
.opt{border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:10px;padding:.55rem .7rem}
.opt.rec{border-color:var(--acc)}
.answered .opt{opacity:.45}
.answered .opt.chosen{opacity:1;border:2px solid var(--ok)}
.badge{font-size:.7rem;padding:.05rem .4rem;border-radius:6px;background:var(--acc);color:#fff;margin-left:.4rem}
.code{font:600 .85rem var(--mono);border:1px solid var(--line);background:var(--bg);color:var(--fg);border-radius:6px;padding:.1rem .45rem;cursor:pointer}
.code.copied{background:var(--ok);border-color:var(--ok);color:#fff}
.pc{list-style:none;padding:0;margin:.3rem 0 0;font-size:.85rem}
.pc li::before{content:"+ ";color:var(--ok);font-weight:700}
.pc li.con::before{content:"\2212  ";color:var(--bad)}
.own{margin-top:.6rem;color:var(--mut);font-size:.88rem}
.ans{margin-top:.6rem;color:var(--ok);font-weight:600}
.empty{color:var(--mut);text-align:center;padding:3rem 0}
.nojs{max-width:640px;margin:3rem auto;padding:16px 20px;background:var(--card);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<header>
  <div class="top"><h1 id="title">Wallpainter</h1><span class="crumb-path" id="path"></span><button class="theme" id="theme" type="button"></button></div>
  <nav id="tabs"></nav>
  <div id="err" hidden></div>
</header>
<div class="nojs" id="nojs">
  <h2>This view cannot load the board</h2>
  <p>You are probably looking at a static preview or copy, for example in an agent's built-in browser. It cannot run the board or reach <code>state.js</code>. Open the board in your system browser:</p>
  <pre><code>open .wallpainter/index.html</code></pre>
  <p>Linux: <code>xdg-open</code>, Windows: <code>start</code>. To show it inside an embedded browser, serve it locally and open <code>http://localhost:8766</code>:</p>
  <pre><code>python3 -m http.server 8766 --bind 127.0.0.1 --directory .wallpainter</code></pre>
</div>
<main id="main"></main>
<script>
"use strict";
document.getElementById("nojs").hidden = true;
const POLL_MS = 2000;
const MERMAID_SRC = "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/mermaid@10.9.1/dist/mermaid.min.js";
const ROW = 28, LANE_GAP = 18, LANE_PAD = 12;
const CLOSED = new Set(["done", "dropped"]);
const STATUS_COLOR = { open: "var(--mut)", active: "var(--acc)", blocked: "var(--bad)", done: "var(--ok)", dropped: "var(--mut)" };
const TEXT = {
  en: { overview: "Overview", path: "Path", next: "Up next", openAsks: "Open decisions", none: "Nothing open.", rec: "recommended", own: "your own solution", chosen: "Chosen", waits: "Waits for", blocks: "Blocks", branched: "New topic", allSteps: "all steps", missing: "state.js not found next to index.html", broken: "state.js has an error - showing the last valid state", empty: "No events yet. The agent appends them to state.js.", status: { open: "open", active: "active", blocked: "blocked", done: "done", dropped: "dropped" }, themeTitle: "Appearance", theme: { auto: "Auto", light: "Light", dark: "Dark" }, structure: "Structure", history: "History", ready: "ready", decide: "decide", close: "close this topic", closedBy: "closed with", legend: "<b>bold</b> = current path · <b>ready</b> = can be worked on now · ◆ open decision · red dashed = waits for" },
  de: { overview: "Übersicht", path: "Pfad", next: "Als Nächstes", openAsks: "Offene Entscheidungen", none: "Nichts offen.", rec: "empfohlen", own: "eigene Lösung", chosen: "Gewählt", waits: "Wartet auf", blocks: "Blockiert", branched: "Neues Thema", allSteps: "alle Schritte", missing: "state.js fehlt neben index.html", broken: "state.js enthält einen Fehler - letzter gültiger Stand wird angezeigt", empty: "Noch keine Einträge. Der Agent schreibt sie nach state.js.", status: { open: "offen", active: "aktiv", blocked: "blockiert", done: "erledigt", dropped: "verworfen" }, themeTitle: "Darstellung", theme: { auto: "Auto", light: "Hell", dark: "Dunkel" }, structure: "Struktur", history: "Verlauf", ready: "bereit", decide: "entscheiden", close: "Thema schließen", closedBy: "geschlossen mit", legend: "<b>fett</b> = aktueller Pfad · <b>bereit</b> = jetzt bearbeitbar · ◆ offene Entscheidung · rot gestrichelt = wartet auf" },
};

const byId = (id) => document.getElementById(id);
const esc = (v) => String(v ?? "").replace(/[&<>"']/g, (c) => ({ "&": "&amp;", "<": "&lt;", ">": "&gt;", '"': "&quot;", "'": "&#39;" })[c]);
const asList = (v) => (v == null ? [] : Array.isArray(v) ? v : [v]);
const short = (s, n = 26) => (String(s).length > n ? String(s).slice(0, n - 1) + "…" : String(s));
const store = (k, v) => { try { localStorage.setItem(k, v); } catch { /* storage unavailable */ } };
const recall = (k) => { try { return localStorage.getItem(k); } catch { return null; } };

const THEMES = ["auto", "light", "dark"];
const systemDark = matchMedia("(prefers-color-scheme: dark)");

let model = fold([]);
let showAll = recall("wp-all") === "1";
let view = recall("wp-view") === "history" ? "history" : "structure";
let theme = THEMES.includes(recall("wp-theme")) ? recall("wp-theme") : "auto";
let seen = 0;
let lastKey = "";
let buffer = [];
let loading = false;
let loadError = "";
let mermaidState = "idle";
const tx = () => TEXT[model.lang] || TEXT.en;
const isFresh = (e) => e._i >= seen;

window.W = (event) => buffer.push(event);
window.addEventListener("error", (ev) => {
  if (loading) loadError = ev.lineno ? `${ev.message} (state.js:${ev.lineno})` : tx().broken;
});

/* ---------- state loading ---------- */
function poll() {
  if (document.hidden || loading) return;
  buffer = []; loadError = ""; loading = true;
  const script = document.createElement("script");
  script.src = `state.js?v=${Date.now()}`;
  script.onload = () => finishLoad(script, "");
  script.onerror = () => finishLoad(script, tx().missing);
  document.head.appendChild(script);
}

function finishLoad(script, missing) {
  script.remove();
  loading = false;
  const error = missing || loadError;
  byId("err").hidden = !error;
  byId("err").textContent = error;
  if (missing && !lastKey) showOpenHint();
  if (error) return;
  byId("nojs").hidden = true;
  const key = JSON.stringify(buffer);
  if (key === lastKey) return;
  seen = lastKey ? model.count : buffer.length;
  lastKey = key;
  model = fold(buffer);
  rerender();
}

/* ---------- theme ---------- */
const isDark = () => theme === "dark" || (theme === "auto" && systemDark.matches);

function applyTheme() {
  if (theme === "auto") delete document.documentElement.dataset.theme;
  else document.documentElement.dataset.theme = theme;
  const button = byId("theme");
  button.textContent = `◐ ${tx().theme[theme]}`;
  button.title = tx().themeTitle;
}

function cycleTheme() {
  theme = THEMES[(THEMES.indexOf(theme) + 1) % THEMES.length];
  store("wp-theme", theme);
  rerender();
}

/* Without a reachable state.js (static preview or data: copy) explain how to open the board. */
function showOpenHint() {
  byId("nojs").hidden = false;
  byId("main").replaceChildren();
}

/* ---------- event folding ---------- */
function fold(events) {
  const m = { title: "Wallpainter", lang: "en", count: events.length, topics: new Map(), asks: new Map(), items: new Map(), deps: [], next: [], focus: null, rows: [] };
  const upsertTopic = (fields) => {
    const t = m.topics.get(fields.id) || { s: "open", log: [], kids: [], _i: -1 };
    Object.assign(t, fields);
    m.topics.set(t.id, t); m.items.set(t.id, t);
    return t;
  };
  const topic = (id) => m.topics.get(id) || upsertTopic({ id, title: id });

  events.forEach((raw, i) => {
    const e = { ...raw, _i: i };
    switch (e.t) {
      case "board": m.title = e.title || m.title; m.lang = e.lang || m.lang; break;
      case "topic": {
        const { t: _type, ...fields } = e;
        upsertTopic(fields);
        m.rows.push({ e, topic: e.id });
        if (e.from) { const parent = topic(e.from); parent.kids.push(e.id); parent.log.push({ t: "branch", ref: e.id, _i: i }); }
        m.focus = m.focus || e.id;
        break;
      }
      case "step": topic(e.in).log.push(e); if (e.id) m.items.set(e.id, e); m.rows.push({ e, topic: e.in, minor: true }); break;
      case "ask": e.answer = null; topic(e.in).log.push(e); m.asks.set(e.id, e); m.items.set(e.id, e); m.rows.push({ e, topic: e.in }); break;
      case "answer": { const ask = m.asks.get(e.d); if (ask) { ask.answer = e; m.rows.push({ e, topic: ask.in }); } break; }
      case "status": {
        const t = topic(e.in);
        t.s = e.s;
        t.closedBy = CLOSED.has(e.s) ? e.by : undefined;
        t.log.push(e);
        m.rows.push({ e, topic: e.in });
        break;
      }
      case "dep": topic(e.on); topic(e.in).log.push(e); m.deps.push(e); m.rows.push({ e, topic: e.in }); break;
      case "focus": topic(e.in); m.focus = e.in; break;
      case "next": m.next = asList(e.items); break;
      case "patch": { const target = m.items.get(e.id); if (target) { const { t: _t, id: _id, _i: _x, ...rest } = e; Object.assign(target, rest); } break; }
    }
  });
  return m;
}

/* A decision is open while unanswered and its topic is not closed. */
const isOpenAsk = (a) => !a.answer && !CLOSED.has(model.topics.get(a.in)?.s);

/* "blocked" backed by deps ends when all those topics are closed;
   "blocked" without deps is an external blocker and stays. */
function effectiveStatus(t) {
  if (t.s !== "blocked") return t.s;
  const deps = model.deps.filter((d) => d.in === t.id);
  return deps.length && deps.every((d) => CLOSED.has(model.topics.get(d.on)?.s)) ? "open" : "blocked";
}

function pathOf(id) {
  const path = [];
  for (let t = model.topics.get(id); t && !path.includes(t.id); t = model.topics.get(t.from)) path.unshift(t.id);
  return path;
}

/* ---------- text rendering ---------- */
function autoLink(html) {
  return html.split(/(<[^>]+>)/).map((part) => (part.startsWith("<") ? part
    : part.replace(/\b([TDS]\d+)\b/g, (id) => (model.items.has(id) ? `<a data-go="${id}">${id}</a>` : id)))).join("");
}

function inline(text) {
  return esc(text).split("`").map((part, i) => (i % 2 ? `<code>${part}</code>` : autoLink(part
    .replace(/\*\*(.+?)\*\*/g, "<b>$1</b>")
    .replace(/\[([^\]]+)\]\(((?:https?:\/\/|\.{0,2}\/)[^)\s]+)\)/g, '<a href="$2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">$1</a>')))).join("");
}

function codeBlock(code, lang) {
  const lines = String(code ?? "").split("\n").map((line) => {
    const cls = lang === "diff" ? (line.startsWith("+") ? "diff-add" : line.startsWith("-") ? "diff-del" : "") : "";
    return cls ? `<span class="${cls}">${esc(line)}</span>` : esc(line);
  });
  return `<pre><code>${lines.join("\n")}</code></pre>`;
}

function table(lines) {
  const rows = lines.filter((l) => !/^[\s|:-]+$/.test(l))
    .map((l) => l.trim().replace(/^\||\|$/g, "").split("|").map((c) => inline(c.trim())));
  const [head = [], ...body] = rows;
  return `<table><tr>${head.map((c) => `<th>${c}</th>`).join("")}</tr>${body.map((r) => `<tr>${r.map((c) => `<td>${c}</td>`).join("")}</tr>`).join("")}</table>`;
}

function md(src) {
  if (!src) return "";
  const out = [];
  let para = [], list = null, code = null, rows = [];
  const flushPara = () => { if (para.length) out.push(`<p>${inline(para.join(" "))}</p>`); para = []; };
  const closeList = () => { if (list) out.push(`</${list}>`); list = null; };
  const flushTable = () => { if (rows.length) out.push(table(rows)); rows = []; };
  for (const line of String(src).split("\n")) {
    if (code) {
      if (line.startsWith("```")) { out.push(codeBlock(code.lines.join("\n"), code.lang)); code = null; } else code.lines.push(line);
      continue;
    }
    if (line.trim().startsWith("|")) { flushPara(); closeList(); rows.push(line); continue; }
    flushTable();
    const fence = line.match(/^```(\w*)/);
    const head = line.match(/^#{1,4}\s+(.*)/);
    const item = line.match(/^\s*([-*]|\d+[.)])\s+(.*)/);
    if (fence) { flushPara(); closeList(); code = { lang: fence[1], lines: [] }; }
    else if (head) { flushPara(); closeList(); out.push(`<h4>${inline(head[1])}</h4>`); }
    else if (item) {
      flushPara();
      const tag = /\d/.test(item[1]) ? "ol" : "ul";
      if (list !== tag) { closeList(); out.push(`<${tag}>`); list = tag; }
      out.push(`<li>${inline(item[2])}</li>`);
    }
    else if (!line.trim()) { flushPara(); closeList(); }
    else { closeList(); para.push(line); }
  }
  if (code) out.push(codeBlock(code.lines.join("\n"), code.lang));
  flushPara(); closeList(); flushTable();
  return out.join("");
}

const link = (id) => `<a data-go="${esc(id)}">${esc(id)}</a>`;
const closeButton = (code) => `<button class="code close-code" data-copy="${esc(code)}" title="${esc(tx().close)}">${esc(code)}</button>`;
const statusChip = (s) => `<span class="s" style="--c:${STATUS_COLOR[s] || "var(--mut)"}">${esc(tx().status[s] || s)}</span>`;

/* ---------- views ---------- */
function rerender() {
  const y = window.scrollY;
  render();
  window.scrollTo(0, y);
}

function render() {
  if (!lastKey) return; // nothing loaded yet: keep the open hint instead of an empty board
  const [view] = location.hash.slice(1).split(":");
  const current = model.topics.has(view) ? view : "overview";
  document.documentElement.lang = model.lang;
  applyTheme();
  document.title = `${model.title} · Wallpainter`;
  byId("title").textContent = model.title;
  const focus = model.topics.get(model.focus);
  byId("path").textContent = focus ? `${tx().path}: ${pathOf(focus.id).join(" › ")} · ${focus.title}` : "";
  byId("tabs").innerHTML = renderTabs(current);
  byId("main").innerHTML = current === "overview" ? renderOverview() : renderTopic(model.topics.get(current));
  runMermaid();
}

function renderTabs(current) {
  const tab = (ref, label, fresh) => `<a href="#${esc(ref)}" class="${ref === current ? "on" : ""}${fresh ? " fresh" : ""}">${label}</a>`;
  const topics = [...model.topics.values()].map((t) => {
    const open = t.log.filter((e) => e.t === "ask" && isOpenAsk(e)).length;
    const label = `<span class="dot" style="--c:${STATUS_COLOR[effectiveStatus(t)] || "var(--mut)"}"></span>${esc(t.id)} ${esc(short(t.title))}${open ? ` <span class="n">${open}</span>` : ""}`;
    return tab(t.id, label, topicIsFresh(t));
  });
  return tab("overview", esc(tx().overview), false) + topics.join("");
}
const topicIsFresh = (t) => isFresh(t) || t.log.some((e) => isFresh(e) || (e.answer && isFresh(e.answer)));

function renderOverview() {
  if (!model.count) return `<p class="empty">${esc(tx().empty)}</p>`;
  const openAsks = [...model.asks.values()].filter(isOpenAsk);
  const asks = openAsks.length ? `<ul>${openAsks.map((a) => `<li><a data-go="${esc(a.id)}"><span class="tag">${esc(a.id)}</span>${inline(a.q)}</a><span class="why">${[...asList(a.opts).map((o) => esc(o.c)), a.own ? `${esc(a.own)} -` : ""].filter(Boolean).join(" · ")}</span></li>`).join("")}</ul>` : `<p class="why">${esc(tx().none)}</p>`;
  const segments = ["structure", "history"].map((v) => `<button type="button" data-view="${v}"${v === view ? ' class="on"' : ""}>${esc(tx()[v])}</button>`).join("");
  const body = view === "history"
    ? `<label class="tg"><input type="checkbox" id="all"${showAll ? " checked" : ""}> ${esc(tx().allSteps)}</label><div class="seg">${segments}</div><div id="graph">${renderGraph()}</div>`
    : `<div class="seg">${segments}</div>${renderTree()}<div class="legend">${tx().legend}</div>`;
  return `<div class="ov">
    <section class="card">${body}</section>
    <aside class="card next"><h2>${esc(tx().next)}</h2>${renderNext()}<h2 style="margin-top:1rem">${esc(tx().openAsks)}</h2>${asks}</aside>
  </div>`;
}

function renderNext() {
  if (!model.next.length) return `<p class="why">${esc(tx().none)}</p>`;
  return `<ol>${model.next.map(({ ref, why }) => {
    const item = model.items.get(ref);
    const stale = item && (item.t === "ask" ? !isOpenAsk(item) : CLOSED.has(item.s));
    return `<li data-ref="${esc(ref)}"${stale ? ' class="stale"' : ""}><a data-go="${esc(ref)}"><span class="tag">${esc(ref)}</span>${inline(item ? item.q || item.title || "" : "")}</a><span class="why">${inline(why || "")}</span></li>`;
  }).join("")}</ol>`;
}

const ARROW_DEFS = `<defs><marker id="arrow" viewBox="0 0 8 8" refX="7" refY="4" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0 0L8 4L0 8z" fill="var(--bad)"/></marker></defs>`;

/* Structure view: problem tree (parent -> sub-topics) with open decisions as leaves,
   dependency arcs in a left gutter, and "ready" marking for unblocked leaf topics. */
function treeNodes() {
  const nodes = [];
  const visited = new Set();
  const visit = (t, depth, parent) => {
    if (visited.has(t.id)) return;
    visited.add(t.id);
    const index = nodes.push({ ref: t.id, topic: t, depth, parent }) - 1;
    t.log.filter((e) => e.t === "ask" && isOpenAsk(e)).forEach((a) => nodes.push({ ref: a.id, ask: a, depth: depth + 1, parent: index }));
    t.kids.forEach((id) => visit(model.topics.get(id), depth + 1, index));
  };
  const topics = [...model.topics.values()];
  topics.filter((t) => !model.topics.has(t.from)).forEach((t) => visit(t, 0, -1));
  topics.forEach((t) => visit(t, 0, -1));
  return nodes;
}

function renderTree() {
  const NODE_ROW = 32, INDENT = 20;
  const isOpen = (id) => !CLOSED.has(model.topics.get(id)?.s);
  const openDeps = model.deps.filter((d) => isOpen(d.in) && isOpen(d.on));
  const waitsOn = (t) => openDeps.filter((d) => d.in === t.id).map((d) => d.on);
  const isReady = (t) => isOpen(t.id) && effectiveStatus(t) !== "blocked" && !waitsOn(t).length && !t.kids.some(isOpen);
  const onPath = new Set(pathOf(model.focus));
  const nodes = treeNodes();
  const row = new Map(nodes.map((n, i) => [n.ref, i]));
  const gutter = openDeps.length ? 6 + openDeps.length * 8 : 0;
  const nx = (depth) => gutter + 10 + depth * INDENT;
  const cy = (i) => i * NODE_ROW + NODE_ROW / 2;
  const parts = [];

  nodes.forEach((n, i) => {
    const x = nx(n.depth), y = cy(i);
    if (n.parent >= 0) {
      const highlight = n.topic && onPath.has(n.ref);
      parts.push(`<path d="M${nx(n.depth - 1)} ${cy(n.parent) + 6} V${y} H${x - 6}" fill="none" stroke="${highlight ? "var(--acc)" : "var(--line)"}" stroke-width="${highlight ? 2.5 : 1.5}"/>`);
    }
    if (n.ask) {
      parts.push(`<path d="M${x} ${y - 6}L${x + 6} ${y}L${x} ${y + 6}L${x - 6} ${y}Z" fill="var(--warn)"/>`);
    } else {
      const status = effectiveStatus(n.topic);
      const color = STATUS_COLOR[status] || "var(--mut)";
      parts.push(`<circle cx="${x}" cy="${y}" r="5" fill="${status === "open" ? "var(--card)" : color}" stroke="${onPath.has(n.ref) ? "var(--acc)" : color}" stroke-width="2"/>`);
    }
  });

  openDeps.forEach((d, k) => {
    const from = row.get(d.in), to = row.get(d.on);
    if (from === undefined || to === undefined) return;
    const gx = 4 + k * 8;
    parts.push(`<path class="dep" d="M${nx(nodes[from].depth) - 8} ${cy(from)} H${gx} V${cy(to)} H${nx(nodes[to].depth) - 9}" fill="none" stroke="var(--bad)" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="3 3" marker-end="url(#arrow)"/>`);
  });

  const words = tx();
  const html = nodes.map((n, i) => {
    const style = `height:${NODE_ROW}px;padding-left:${nx(n.depth) + 12}px`;
    if (n.ask) {
      const codes = [...asList(n.ask.opts).map((o) => o.c), n.ask.own ? `${n.ask.own} -` : ""].filter(Boolean).map(esc).join(" · ");
      return `<div class="node${isFresh(n.ask) ? " fresh" : ""}" data-ref="${esc(n.ref)}" data-go="${esc(n.ref)}" data-depth="${n.depth}" style="${style}"><span class="tag">${esc(n.ref)}</span><span class="t">${esc(n.ask.q)}</span><span class="codes">${codes}</span><span class="chip" style="--c:var(--warn)">${esc(words.decide)}</span></div>`;
    }
    const t = n.topic;
    const waits = waitsOn(t);
    const classes = [
      onPath.has(t.id) && "onpath", t.id === model.focus && "focus", isReady(t) && "ready",
      CLOSED.has(t.s) && "closed", t.s === "dropped" && "dropped", isFresh(t) && "fresh",
    ].filter(Boolean).join(" ");
    const chip = (text, color, cls = "") => `<span class="chip ${cls}" style="--c:${color}">${esc(text)}</span>`;
    const chips = isReady(t) ? chip(words.ready, "var(--ok)", "ready")
      : waits.length ? chip(`${words.waits} ${waits.join(", ")}`, "var(--bad)", "wait")
      : effectiveStatus(t) !== "open" ? chip(words.status[effectiveStatus(t)] || t.s, STATUS_COLOR[effectiveStatus(t)] || "var(--mut)") : "";
    const closeCode = t.close && !CLOSED.has(t.s) ? closeButton(t.close) : "";
    return `<div class="node ${classes}" data-ref="${esc(t.id)}" data-go="${esc(t.id)}" data-depth="${n.depth}" style="${style}"><span class="tag">${esc(t.id)}</span><span class="t">${esc(t.title)}</span>${closeCode}${chips}</div>`;
  }).join("");

  const width = nx(Math.max(0, ...nodes.map((n) => n.depth))) + 10;
  return `<div id="tree"><svg width="${width}" height="${nodes.length * NODE_ROW}" aria-hidden="true">${ARROW_DEFS}${parts.join("")}</svg>${html}</div>`;
}

/* History view: git-style lanes in chronological order. */
function layoutLanes(rows) {
  const span = new Map();
  rows.forEach((r, y) => { const s = span.get(r.topic); if (s) s.end = y; else span.set(r.topic, { start: y, end: y }); });
  const laneEnds = [];
  for (const [id, s] of span) {
    const t = model.topics.get(id);
    if (!CLOSED.has(t.s)) s.end = rows.length - 1;
    s.merge = CLOSED.has(t.s) && span.has(t.from);
    let lane = laneEnds.findIndex((end) => end < s.start);
    if (lane < 0) lane = laneEnds.length;
    laneEnds[lane] = s.end + (s.merge ? 1 : 0);
    s.lane = lane;
  }
  return { span, laneCount: Math.max(laneEnds.length, 1) };
}

function renderGraph() {
  const rows = model.rows.filter((r) => showAll || !r.minor);
  const { span, laneCount } = layoutLanes(rows);
  const onPath = new Set(pathOf(model.focus));
  const x = (id) => LANE_PAD + span.get(id).lane * LANE_GAP;
  const cy = (y) => y * ROW + ROW / 2;
  const width = LANE_PAD * 2 + (laneCount - 1) * LANE_GAP;
  const parts = [];

  for (const [id, s] of span) {
    const t = model.topics.get(id);
    const color = onPath.has(id) ? "var(--acc)" : STATUS_COLOR[t.s] || "var(--mut)";
    const stroke = `stroke="${color}" stroke-width="${onPath.has(id) ? 3 : 2}" fill="none"${t.s === "dropped" ? ' stroke-dasharray="4 3"' : ""}`;
    const px = span.has(t.from) ? x(t.from) : null;
    const lx = x(id), y0 = cy(s.start), y1 = cy(s.end);
    let d = px !== null && s.start > 0
      ? `M${px} ${y0 - ROW} C${px} ${y0 - ROW / 2} ${lx} ${y0 - ROW / 2} ${lx} ${y0} V${y1}`
      : `M${lx} ${y0} V${y1}`;
    if (s.merge) d += ` C${lx} ${y1 + ROW / 2} ${px} ${y1 + ROW / 2} ${px} ${y1 + ROW}`;
    parts.push(`<path class="lane" d="${d}" ${stroke}/>`);
  }

  rows.forEach((r, y) => {
    const e = r.e, cx = x(r.topic), c = cy(y);
    if (e.t === "dep" && span.has(e.on)) {
      parts.push(`<path d="M${cx} ${c} H${x(e.on)}" stroke="var(--bad)" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="3 3" marker-end="url(#arrow)"/>`);
    }
    const fill = { topic: "var(--card)", ask: e.answer ? "var(--ok)" : "var(--warn)", answer: "var(--ok)", status: STATUS_COLOR[e.s], dep: "var(--card)" }[e.t] || "var(--mut)";
    const stroke = onPath.has(r.topic) ? "var(--acc)" : STATUS_COLOR[model.topics.get(r.topic).s] || "var(--mut)";
    parts.push(`<circle cx="${cx}" cy="${c}" r="${r.minor ? 3 : 5}" fill="${fill}" stroke="${stroke}" stroke-width="2"/>`);
  });

  const svg = `<svg width="${width}" height="${(rows.length + 1) * ROW}" aria-hidden="true">${ARROW_DEFS}${parts.join("")}</svg>`;
  const labels = rows.map((r) => `<div class="row${isFresh(r.e) ? " fresh" : ""}" data-go="${esc(rowTarget(r))}" style="height:${ROW}px;line-height:${ROW}px;padding-left:${width + 6}px"><span class="tag">${esc(r.topic)}</span>${rowLabel(r.e)}</div>`);
  return svg + labels.join("") + `<div style="height:${ROW}px"></div>`;
}

function rowTarget({ e, topic }) {
  if (e.t === "ask") return e.id;
  if (e.t === "answer") return e.d;
  if (e.t === "step" && e.id) return e.id;
  return topic;
}

function rowLabel(e) {
  const t = tx();
  switch (e.t) {
    case "topic": return `⎇ ${esc(e.title)}`;
    case "step": return esc(e.title || e.kind || "");
    case "ask": return `? ${esc(e.q)}`;
    case "answer": {
      const option = asList(model.asks.get(e.d)?.opts).find((o) => o.c === e.c);
      return `✓ ${esc(e.d)} → ${esc(e.c || "")} ${esc(option ? option.h : e.note || "")}`;
    }
    case "status": return `${esc(t.status[e.s] || e.s)}${e.note ? ` – ${esc(e.note)}` : ""}`;
    case "dep": return `${esc(t.waits)} ${esc(e.on)}`;
    default: return "";
  }
}

function renderTopic(t) {
  const words = tx();
  const waits = model.deps.filter((d) => d.in === t.id).map((d) => link(d.on));
  const blocks = model.deps.filter((d) => d.on === t.id).map((d) => link(d.in));
  const deps = [waits.length ? `${esc(words.waits)}: ${waits.join(", ")}` : "", blocks.length ? `${esc(words.blocks)}: ${blocks.join(", ")}` : ""].filter(Boolean).join(" · ");
  const crumbs = pathOf(t.id).map((id) => `${link(id)} ${esc(short(model.topics.get(id).title, 18))}`).join(" › ");
  const closer = CLOSED.has(t.s)
    ? (t.closedBy ? `<div class="closer closed-by">${esc(words.closedBy)} <code>${esc(t.closedBy)}</code></div>` : "")
    : (t.close ? `<div class="closer">${closeButton(t.close)} ${esc(words.close)}</div>` : "");
  return `<div class="card head"><div class="crumbs">${crumbs}</div><h2>${esc(t.title)}${statusChip(t.s)}</h2>${md(t.md)}${deps ? `<div class="deps">${deps}</div>` : ""}${closer}</div>
    <ol class="tl">${t.log.map(renderItem).join("")}</ol>`;
}

function renderItem(e) {
  const words = tx();
  const fresh = isFresh(e) || (e.answer && isFresh(e.answer)) ? " fresh" : "";
  const mini = (html, color, cls = "") => `<li class="mini ${cls}${fresh}" style="--c:${color}">${html}</li>`;
  switch (e.t) {
    case "branch": return mini(`⎇ ${esc(words.branched)}: ${link(e.ref)} ${esc(model.topics.get(e.ref)?.title || "")}`, "var(--acc)", "branch");
    case "status": return mini(`${statusChip(e.s)}${e.by ? ` <code>${esc(e.by)}</code>` : ""}${e.note ? ` ${inline(e.note)}` : ""}`, STATUS_COLOR[e.s] || "var(--mut)");
    case "dep": return mini(`${esc(words.waits)} ${link(e.on)}${e.note ? ` – ${inline(e.note)}` : ""}`, "var(--bad)");
    case "ask": return `<li class="${fresh}" style="--c:var(--warn)">${renderAsk(e)}</li>`;
    default: return `<li class="${fresh}"${e.id ? ` id="${esc(e.id)}"` : ""} style="--c:${e.kind === "result" ? "var(--ok)" : "var(--acc)"}"><div class="card${e.kind === "result" ? " result" : ""}"><span class="kind">${esc(e.kind || "note")}</span>${e.title ? `<h3>${esc(e.title)}</h3>` : ""}${renderBody(e)}</div></li>`;
  }
}

function renderBody(e) {
  switch (e.kind) {
    case "compare": return `<div class="cmp">${[e.a, e.b].map((side) => `<div><h4>${esc(side?.h || "")}</h4>${md(side?.md)}</div>`).join("")}</div>${md(e.md)}`;
    case "diagram": return `<div class="mermaid">${esc(e.mermaid)}</div>${md(e.md)}`;
    case "code": return codeBlock(e.code, e.lang) + md(e.md);
    default: return md(e.md);
  }
}

function renderAsk(a) {
  const words = tx();
  const chosen = a.answer?.c;
  const prosCons = (o) => {
    const items = [...asList(o.pro).map((v) => `<li>${inline(v)}</li>`), ...asList(o.con).map((v) => `<li class="con">${inline(v)}</li>`)];
    return items.length ? `<ul class="pc">${items.join("")}</ul>` : "";
  };
  const opts = asList(a.opts).map((o) => `<div class="opt${o.rec ? " rec" : ""}${o.c === chosen ? " chosen" : ""}"><button class="code" data-copy="${esc(o.c)}">${esc(o.c)}</button> <b>${esc(o.h || "")}</b>${o.rec ? `<span class="badge">${esc(words.rec)}</span>` : ""}${md(o.md)}${prosCons(o)}</div>`).join("");
  const own = a.own ? `<div class="own"><button class="code" data-copy="${esc(a.own)} - ">${esc(a.own)}</button> - ${esc(words.own)}</div>` : "";
  const answer = a.answer ? `<div class="ans">✓ ${esc(words.chosen)}: ${esc(a.answer.c || "")}${a.answer.note ? ` – ${inline(a.answer.note)}` : ""}</div>` : "";
  return `<div class="card ask${a.answer ? " answered" : ""}" id="${esc(a.id)}"><div class="q"><span class="tag">${esc(a.id)}</span>${inline(a.q)}</div>${md(a.md)}<div class="opts">${opts}</div>${own}${answer}</div>`;
}

function runMermaid() {
  const nodes = [...document.querySelectorAll(".mermaid:not([data-processed])")];
  if (!nodes.length || mermaidState === "loading" || mermaidState === "failed") return;
  if (mermaidState === "ready") {
    window.mermaid.initialize({ startOnLoad: false, theme: isDark() ? "dark" : "default" });
    window.mermaid.run({ nodes }).catch(() => {});
    return;
  }
  mermaidState = "loading";
  const script = document.createElement("script");
  script.src = MERMAID_SRC;
  script.onload = () => { mermaidState = "ready"; runMermaid(); };
  script.onerror = () => { mermaidState = "failed"; };
  document.head.appendChild(script);
}

/* ---------- interaction ---------- */
function goTo(ref) {
  const item = model.items.get(ref);
  if (!item) return;
  const topicId = model.topics.has(ref) ? ref : item.in;
  const hash = topicId === ref ? `#${topicId}` : `#${topicId}:${ref}`;
  if (location.hash === hash) scrollToAnchor(); else location.hash = hash;
}

function scrollToAnchor() {
  const anchor = location.hash.split(":")[1];
  const el = anchor && byId(anchor);
  if (el) el.scrollIntoView({ block: "center" }); else window.scrollTo(0, 0);
}

function copyCode(button) {
  const done = () => { button.classList.add("copied"); setTimeout(() => button.classList.remove("copied"), 900); };
  navigator.clipboard?.writeText(button.dataset.copy).then(done, () => {});
}

function switchView(next) {
  view = next;
  store("wp-view", view);
  rerender();
}

document.addEventListener("click", (ev) => {
  const target = ev.target.closest("[data-go],[data-copy],[data-view]");
  if (!target) return;
  ev.preventDefault();
  if (target.dataset.go) goTo(target.dataset.go);
  else if (target.dataset.view) switchView(target.dataset.view);
  else copyCode(target);
});
document.addEventListener("change", (ev) => {
  if (ev.target.id !== "all") return;
  showAll = ev.target.checked;
  store("wp-all", showAll ? "1" : "");
  rerender();
});
byId("theme").addEventListener("click", cycleTheme);
systemDark.addEventListener("change", () => { if (theme === "auto") rerender(); });
window.addEventListener("hashchange", () => { render(); scrollToAnchor(); });
document.addEventListener("visibilitychange", poll);
applyTheme();
poll();
setInterval(poll, POLL_MS);
</script>
</body>
</html>
<!-- wallpainter:viewer:end -->
```
